    {
      "id": "calculus-002",
      "sha256": "86c6d4a82d751b103ebd1fb01c12f25dcd8dbd8a3e181cf918b543fd92076b7a",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 3,
      "raw": "在2500年前，古希腊人把一个多边形分成三角形，并把它们的面积相加，才找到计算多边形面积的方法。\n为了求出曲线形状（比如圆）的面积，古希腊人在这样的形状上刻内接多边形。\n如 [原文引用：fig_circle_area](https://zh.d2l.ai/chapter_preliminaries/calculus.html)所示，内接多边形的等长边越多，就越接近圆。\n这个过程也被称为*逼近法*（method of exhaustion）。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-003",
      "sha256": "806d4627779e14bc8349f5a394d672e577bf7676b92d06824fa3de1c00c7f521",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 8,
      "raw": "![用逼近法求圆的面积](../img/polygon-circle.svg)",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-004",
      "sha256": "c692ec700ca068996b691758440f75a65a4a5b2be62b498b0871d6b074e0cf64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 10,
      "raw": "事实上，逼近法就是*积分*（integral calculus）的起源。\n2000多年后，微积分的另一支，*微分*（differential calculus）被发明出来。\n在微分学最重要的应用是优化问题，即考虑如何把事情做到最好。\n正如在 [原文引用：subsec_norms_and_objectives](https://zh.d2l.ai/chapter_preliminaries/calculus.html)中讨论的那样，\n这种问题在深度学习中是无处不在的。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-005",
      "sha256": "2df72f30a520a2ced200219bf7c6c89b9c5caa7847ea4dd8c6588af776062765",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 16,
      "raw": "在深度学习中，我们“训练”模型，不断更新它们，使它们在看到越来越多的数据时变得越来越好。\n通常情况下，变得更好意味着最小化一个*损失函数*（loss function），\n即一个衡量“模型有多糟糕”这个问题的分数。\n最终，我们真正关心的是生成一个模型，它能够在从未见过的数据上表现良好。\n但“训练”模型只能将模型与我们实际能看到的数据相拟合。\n因此，我们可以将拟合模型的任务分解为两个关键问题：",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-006",
      "sha256": "459cd3035c01edc6705d8468db0d033b067023dc4967484ec76c04488d7f58dc",
      "type": "list",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 23,
      "raw": "* *优化*（optimization）：用模型拟合观测数据的过程；\n* *泛化*（generalization）：数学原理和实践者的智慧，能够指导我们生成出有效性超出用于训练的数据集本身的模型。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-007",
      "sha256": "6faa3fe5954fc32787cb163bdaff14d5a3052599af9b7021b5cc34b0819c07fe",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 26,
      "raw": "为了帮助读者在后面的章节中更好地理解优化问题和方法，\n本节提供了一个非常简短的入门教程，帮助读者快速掌握深度学习中常用的微分知识。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-008",
      "sha256": "aaed6afbd859a443ebeebf7ed5f971f7d87fa8f0492cc6abec5e9fea63448996",
      "type": "heading",
      "depth": 2,
      "line": 29,
      "raw": "## 导数和微分",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-009",
      "sha256": "a78b3b773b178a5fabcb7b65f2886d44042f8a9b053463de4f87d64f549fac38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 31,
      "raw": "我们首先讨论导数的计算，这是几乎所有深度学习优化算法的关键步骤。\n在深度学习中，我们通常选择对于模型参数可微的损失函数。\n简而言之，对于每个参数，\n如果我们把这个参数*增加*或*减少*一个无穷小的量，可以知道损失会以多快的速度增加或减少，",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-010",
      "sha256": "31e37ed769bdfdf6edc531a42bc2ea563ab34a3787f96287c6e8af7fdc35cd90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 36,
      "raw": "假设我们有一个函数$f: \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$，其输入和输出都是标量。\n**如果$f$的*导数*存在，这个极限被定义为**",
      "math": {
        "expected": 2,
        "rendered": 2,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-011",
      "sha256": "7fb5a98de31c3af9ea1009f85cb5269734a9d8f62fa773fb6fd2a34f01e6fe4c",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 39,
      "raw": "**$$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}.$$**",
      "math": {
        "expected": 1,
        "rendered": 1,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-012",
      "sha256": "3ee16121aa2e2bc7a595da750fbd180aad4a4226003f28253ecba78f77463204",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 41,
      "raw": "如果$f'(a)$存在，则称$f$在$a$处是*可微*（differentiable）的。\n如果$f$在一个区间内的每个数上都是可微的，则此函数在此区间中是可微的。\n我们可以将 [原文引用：eq_derivative](https://zh.d2l.ai/chapter_preliminaries/calculus.html)中的导数$f'(x)$解释为$f(x)$相对于$x$的*瞬时*（instantaneous）变化率。\n所谓的瞬时变化率是基于$x$中的变化$h$，且$h$接近$0$。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 11,
        "rendered": 11,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-013",
      "sha256": "29299d9eeb9fb63dfd463d7125e6f0137ed3bb42911dd22f5ec203e095916ee7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 46,
      "raw": "为了更好地解释导数，让我们做一个实验。\n**定义$u=f(x)=3x^2-4x$**如下：",
      "math": {
        "expected": 1,
        "rendered": 1,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-014",
      "sha256": "13f9a0422aba93e93c4739bb2a9e9af9ae23372ee20fe055d9c4d6f2cd49c744",
      "type": "code",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 60,
      "raw": "```python\n%matplotlib inline\nfrom d2l import torch as d2l\nfrom matplotlib_inline import backend_inline\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef f(x):\n    return 3 * x ** 2 - 4 * x\n```",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-015",
      "sha256": "ff152f05043b67c9d0de662d7b1e2ed70723d8dbbf47a0c981cf026cc6a70db6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 92,
      "raw": "**通过令$x=1$并让$h$接近$0$，** [原文引用：eq_derivative](https://zh.d2l.ai/chapter_preliminaries/calculus.html)中**$\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}$的数值结果接近$2$**。\n虽然这个实验不是一个数学证明，但稍后会看到，当$x=1$时，导数$u'$是$2$。",
      "math": {
        "expected": 8,
        "rendered": 8,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-016",
      "sha256": "04ddaf9a40a5e2861468e0c09fffe1b29e593e927eb9b65e144a61964dbd2665",
      "type": "code",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 95,
      "raw": "```python\ndef numerical_lim(f, x, h):\n    return (f(x + h) - f(x)) / h\n\nh = 0.1\nfor i in range(5):\n    print(f'h={h:.5f}, numerical limit={numerical_lim(f, 1, h):.5f}')\n    h *= 0.1\n```",
      "math": {
        "expected": 0,
        "rendered": 0,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-017",
      "sha256": "8c45e4ad800cb22e26d0ff54b3e8fcd0151569cc7295bb35e721fc96f1de6afb",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 105,
      "raw": "让我们熟悉一下导数的几个等价符号。\n给定$y=f(x)$，其中$x$和$y$分别是函数$f$的自变量和因变量。以下表达式是等价的：",
      "math": {
        "expected": 4,
        "rendered": 4,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-018",
      "sha256": "6b01f6d060a4fd152a677403682dabec9066721893565b4578a3302f03f84448",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 108,
      "raw": "$$f'(x) = y' = \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{df}{dx} = \\frac{d}{dx} f(x) = Df(x) = D_x f(x),$$",
      "math": {
        "expected": 1,
        "rendered": 1,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-019",
      "sha256": "f1e7dfae21f514ee5fbda548b26f0a7f3062a319c037bee83a2026eb6a85c5f6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "depth": null,
      "line": 110,
      "raw": "其中符号$\\frac{d}{dx}$和$D$是*微分运算符*，表示*微分*操作。\n我们可以使用以下规则来对常见函数求微分：",
      "math": {
        "expected": 2,
        "rendered": 2,
        "errors": 0,
        "pending": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-020",
